 write_text(ROOT/"SHARED_MAP_SEARCH.md",intro+"One final synthesis candidate mapped `S_CAUSAL_PANEL_V1` to a generic physical apparatus record: geometry, event payload, material response and history. It was rejected as a shared external Rosetta because a generic detector architecture explains the same structure, no cross-sector unit conversion is identifiable, and no unused numerical external relation follows.\n")
 write_text(ROOT/"FINAL_ROSETTA_ATTEMPT.md",intro+"Exactly one final synthesis attempt was made after the native graph and fingerprints were frozen. Calibration subset: transport timing, interface response and ensemble contraction. Candidate: a zero-label causal-record map. Competitors: generic detector, ballistic transport, independent interface threshold and independent relaxation models. The independent models fit with equal or greater specificity; the shared map made no unused quantitative external prediction. Outcome: `MULTI_RELATION_INTERNAL_CONVERGENCE`, not a shared external map.\n")
 write_text(ROOT/"FINAL_EXTERNAL_FALSIFICATION_PROTOCOL.md",intro+"Future test: first identify one physical apparatus where the same preparation/measurement map jointly predicts (1) path delay, (2) phase/history-conditioned pile-up or exclusion, and (3) organization-dependent capture using one frozen calibration. Units, uncertainty and detector dead-time must be preregistered; a held-out geometry must be predicted without refit. Failure of any relation falsifies the proposed shared map while leaving internal DEE laws intact.\n")
 write_text(ROOT/"ROSETTA_STATUS.md",intro+"Highest status: `MULTI_RELATION_INTERNAL_CONVERGENCE`. CORE13's event-sector structural candidate remains sectorial. CORE15 supplies no shared low-parameter external map, unused external prediction or external holdout.\n")
